const teaching=`<p class="lead">Teaching, adding an executable capability, granting authority and validating a result are different changes. Here is where each belongs in the current source-built ARTEX.</p><div class="domain-grid">${seams.map(s=>`<article class="domain"><span class="eyebrow">${esc(s.id)}</span><h3>${esc(s.name)}</h3><p class="question">${esc(s.purpose)}</p><p>${esc(s.native)}</p><code>${esc(s.source)}</code><p class="limit">${esc(s.limit)}</p></article>`).join('')}</div><div class="takeaway-block"><b>Start with three local method drafts:</b> a research-and-hypothesis skill; a fresh positive/control reviewer procedure; and an evidence-preserving report/retest procedure. Bind them to the relevant native roles only after review. These are proposed local drafts—not uploaded skills or changed prompts.</div><h3>Routing and priorities across every dossier</h3><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Research item</th><th>Primary destination</th><th>Consumer</th><th>Priority / readiness</th></tr></thead><tbody>${projects.map(p=>{const r=routes[p.id];return `<tr><th><a href="#project-${p.id}">${esc(p.name)}</a></th><td>${esc(seams.find(s=>s.id===r.destination).name)}</td><td>${esc(r.consumer)}</td><td><b>${r.priority}</b> · ${esc(r.disposition)}</td></tr>`;}).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p class="caption">P0: establish trustworthy baseline and execution/accounting first. P1: high-value procedure/evidence improvement. P2: conditional specialization or measured method experiment. P3: research-only/defer until relevant scope. These are priority judgments, not measured benefit scores.</p><p>Open “Put this in…” in any project dossier for the exact destination, consumer, native overlap, required inputs, confidence, limits and validation. ${sourceButton('@docs/SYNAPSE-PLATFORM.md','Maintained canonical mapping')}</p><div class="live-note"><b>Specific boundaries from the current source</b><p>Categories organize tasks; they do not teach an agent. Templates preserve description/goal, optional category and task interception rules—not every runtime setting. Skills/prompts do not retrain weights. A custom command needs its binary in the KrisPC execution environment; a Windows installation is not automatically in the Linux container. The bridge supplies model decisions; ARTEX executes the tool calls. A future knowledge service can be one bounded custom wrapper or one MCP integration if native context is insufficient; neither is currently installed by this report.</p></div>`;
mappedHtml=mappedHtml.replace('<section class="chapter" id="experiments"',chapter('06b','teaching','Where to teach and extend ARTEX','Exact destinations, consumers, dependencies and priorities—mapped to the real source.',teaching)+'<section class="chapter" id="experiments"');
