const skillPanel=`<h3>The native skill catalog: three source-bundled packages</h3><div class="version-lanes" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr))"><article><span>API-RECON</span><h4>Frontend / API surface</h4><p>Staged static and dynamic reconnaissance. Uses client-side hooks and mock/stub responses for some route discovery. Explicitly separates reconnaissance from vulnerability/exploitation testing.</p><button class="source-link" data-source="primary/Bundled api-recon boundary">Read the actual boundary ›</button></article><article><span>PLAYWRIGHT-CLI</span><h4>Browser procedure</h4><p>CLI interaction and session guidance. File presence is not a working browser, installed dependency or active role assignment. PC actions still use the existing computeruse harness.</p><button class="source-link" data-source="primary/Bundled browser procedure">Read source instructions ›</button></article><article><span>SCOPESENTRY</span><h4>External service guide</h4><p>Assumes an already deployed ScopeSentry MCP. It describes how to connect and use it; it does not establish that the service is installed, enabled or connected.</p><button class="source-link" data-source="primary/Bundled ScopeSentry prerequisite">Read the prerequisite ›</button></article></div><p>Reed independently inventoried these tracked packages; Delta checked the tracked file list and source excerpts. This is the <b>bundled source catalog</b>, not an inventory of active runtime-visible skills. General-purpose execution can do more than this catalog describes.</p><div class="takeaway-block"><b>A concrete method gap:</b> a curated identity/tenant verification method, business-rule sequence method, strongest-counterexample reviewer and loss-aware report/retest procedure are not supplied by these three packages as a comprehensive library. They can be adapted from our research into native skills/roles without another engine.</div><div class="native-status"><article><span class="eyebrow">METHOD / CATALOG GAP</span><h3>Teach a missing procedure</h3><p>The reviewed bundled catalog does not supply the particular methodology. Prepare a concise sourced skill or role procedure.</p></article><article><span class="eyebrow">CONFIGURATION GAP</span><h3>Connect what already exists</h3><p>A native mechanism exists, but visibility, service, executable or credential availability is unknown. Inspect before adding software.</p></article><article><span class="eyebrow">VALIDATION GAP</span><h3>Prove the outcome</h3><p>Source contains an implementation, but real discovery, effect, stop, export or repair has not been established. A test is needed, not automatically a new feature.</p></article></div>`;
mappedHtml=mappedHtml.replace('<h3>Routing and priorities across every dossier</h3>',skillPanel+'<h3>Routing and priorities across every dossier</h3>');
const codeGap=`<div class="live-note"><b>A concrete code gap that a skill cannot repair</b><p>Hiro's saved deterministic receipt injects an ordinary runner error labeled “SIMULATED provider policy refusal”; the bridge responds HTTP 502 / provider_error with generic message. Delta read that receipt and the actual runner/server paths. This proves loss of generic error classification, <b>not a live refusal or native refusal-payload reproduction</b>. The source separately discards Codex/Claude failure detail. Destination: a small bridge error-contract change with sanitized terminal/retry classification tests; no permission expansion or refusal-evading provider switch. Profiles being pool-excluded do not support an active fallback claim.</p>${sourceButton('@C:/Users/kotar/githubprojects/security/work/audit-receipts/bridge-error-classification-2026-10-21.json','Original mock receipt')}<button class="source-link" data-source="primary/Bridge result classification">Read runner source ›</button> <button class="source-link" data-source="primary/Bridge HTTP error contract">Read HTTP error contract ›</button></div>`;
