const comparative=`<h3>How external approaches test—and what their results mean</h3><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Approach / project</th><th>Access and method</th><th>Reported or observed result</th><th>What transfers to ARTEX</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>PentestGPT</th><td>Historical paper, legacy assistant and maintained two-role framework are different versions/access conditions.</td><td>README labels December 2025 XBOW 90/104 as historical/reference-only. Our own receipts test state, trace, compiler and oracle mechanics with scripted backends.</td><td>Canonical state/recovery discipline. No current framework or ARTEX discovery percentage follows.</td></tr><tr><th>Shannon OSS</th><td>Source plus running URL; maintainer Photoview comparison supplies source/admin credentials, three single-model runs and optional SAST.</td><td>Maintainer-authored selected-app comparison, with retrospective patched-issue set and acknowledged false positive. Not reproduced here.</td><td>Source-to-runtime hypotheses, partial states and output discipline; compare only against an equivalent source-assisted arm.</td></tr><tr><th>Decepticon</th><td>Assisted challenge evaluation with vulnerability tags/hints and multiple cycles.</td><td>Maintainer index: 102/104, cycle-4 final. Winning aggregation is not first-attempt held-out accuracy.</td><td>Prerequisites, explicit blocked outcomes and fresh comparable controls; no universal ranking.</td></tr><tr><th>hackingBuddyGPT / research PentestAgent</th><td>Small Linux/API/AD use cases or product/PoC/advisory-assisted stage pipelines; assumed access differs by mode.</td><td>Paper and source modes differ; our review did not reproduce their headline results or measure an unfamiliar URL-only assessment.</td><td>Bounded task/context experiments and applicable technical retrieval; preserve hints and access as experimental inputs.</td></tr><tr><th>Scanner / conventional tool work</th><td>Map behavior, select an applicable rule or hypothesis, capture exact output, reproduce the meaningful effect and review.</td><td>Selected local ZAP/native adapter/known-answer experiments are real but narrow. Template alerts, signatures and fingerprints remain candidates.</td><td>Specialists answer a specific observation gap; human/domain policy and controls decide the consequence.</td></tr><tr><th>Our owned rehearsal</th><td>Guided known-answer registration/mail/order controls; declared synthetic policy.</td><td>Actual local exchanges and teardown observed; no ARTEX autonomous discovery or blind score.</td><td>Useful development/evidence infrastructure for an ARTEX baseline, with stronger evaluation still needed.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="caption">The linked project dossiers and original studies retain exact source pins and access/benchmark qualifications. No cross-project percentage comparison is justified by these unlike setups.</p>`;
